# Theorem 1. Residual permutation sign cancellation

Let m be a positive integer and let a and b be permutations of {1,...,m}.
Write A_0=B_0=0, A_i=a_1+...+a_i and B_i=b_1+...+b_i.
For a fixed a, let L(a) consist of the permutations b satisfying
A_{i-1}<B_i<=A_i for every i=1,...,m.
Then the sum of sign(b) over b in L(a) is 1 if a=(1,...,m), and 0 otherwise.
Here sign is the usual parity sign of a permutation.
